<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<ValidationRule xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT, NOT IN <description>, AND IT MUST STAY THAT WAY.
        ValidationRule.Description is capped at 255 characters. The full rationale below is
        operationally important, so it was moved here rather than trimmed; a comment is
        repo-only and is never sent to the Metadata API, so it can be as long as it needs to
        be. Do not paste this back into <description>.

        PHASE 2 (2026-08-14): THE GATED STAGE WAS RENAMED 'PSA' -> 'Under Contract (PSA)'.
        Only the stage VALUE moved. The rule name, the gate and its remedy are unchanged, and
        the API name deliberately still reads _Before_PSA - renaming a ValidationRule is a
        delete-and-recreate, and the new value still contains "PSA".

        Stage gate (b): a deal cannot enter Under Contract (PSA) until an APPROVED LOI is in
        place, not merely
        a linked one. "In place" is read as LOI_Approved__c = true, the flag set by
        LOI_Approval's Set_LOI_Approved_Flag final action, the only machine-readable evidence
        the LOI approval happened, since the collapsed single LOI stage does not change
        StageName on approval.

        Gate applies to the stage transition only (ISCHANGED); existing records already at
        Under Contract (PSA) are unaffected.

        MIGRATION SAFETY - MEASURED FROM THIS FORMULA, NOT ASSUMED. The P2 backfill that
        rewrites live rows from 'PSA' to 'Under Contract (PSA)' runs BETWEEN P2-D1 and
        P2-D2, i.e. while this file still reads ISPICKVAL(StageName, 'PSA'). The backfill
        sets the NEW value, which does not match that literal, so this rule cannot fire on
        it. That is why the migration needs no rule deactivation - and why repointing this
        file BEFORE the backfill would break it.
    -->
    <fullName>Approved_LOI_Before_PSA</fullName>
    <active>true</active>
    <description>Blocks stage entry to Under Contract (PSA) unless an approved LOI (LOI_Approved__c) is in place, not merely a linked one. See the XML comment in this file for full rationale.</description>
    <errorConditionFormula>AND(
    ISCHANGED(StageName),
    ISPICKVAL(StageName, &apos;Under Contract (PSA)&apos;),
    OR(
        ISBLANK(Primary_LOI__c),
        NOT(LOI_Approved__c)
    )
)</errorConditionFormula>
    <errorDisplayField>StageName</errorDisplayField>
    <errorMessage>This deal cannot enter Under Contract (PSA) until an approved LOI is in place. Link the primary LOI and complete the LOI approval first.</errorMessage>
</ValidationRule>
